anya_cs: Drafting a short, customer-facing runbook for low-token-budget customers (small pilot customers who care about cost). Goal: one-pager CSM can paste into kickoff email. Comments welcome.

zoe_se: nice. keep the CSM checklist tiny. add an explicit "cost guardrails" bullet so customers know how we limit runaway spend.

anya_cs: good call. initial CSM checklist (pasteable):
- confirm token budget and expected QPS for pilot (CSM note)
- enable lightweight prefill for demo flows (TTL tuned to idle; default 20s)
- set batching target small (batch size 4) to avoid token spikes during demos
- enable streaming with short-window increments to reduce repeated prompt tokens
- turn on cost-guard: max_tokens_per_request = 256 and daily token cap = customer budget
- collect 3 canonical prompts + expected outputs for eval and cost estimate

kartik_sre: add quick SRE mitigation steps if costs spike: 1) throttle prefill, 2) reduce batch size, 3) enable aggressive caching, 4) temporarily enforce stricter token caps.

zoe_se: pasteable client snippet for prefetching + streaming fallback to share with customers:

```
// tiny client prefetch + streaming fallback
async function requestWithFallback(prompt) {
  if (client.canStream()) {
    return client.stream(prompt, {window: 64});
  }
  if (prefill.isReadyFor(prompt)) {
    return client.applyPrefill(prompt);
  }
  return client.requestSync(prompt, {max_tokens: 256});
}
```

rafa_pm: add a short VOC ask: "Which 1-2 flows must keep latency < 2s and accuracy > 90%?" We'll use that to prioritize caching. Also define RenewalRisk signal: pilot exceeds budget twice in 14d OR repeated accuracy complaints -> tag RenewalRisk and escalate.

anya_cs: added VOC line and RenewalRisk rule. final publish ask: thumbs up to add to shared playbooks and paste into the low-touch onboarding kit?

